WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.370
Power stations, cars and homes
run largely on three fossil fuels:

2
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:08.010
coal, oil and natural gas.

3
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:13.250
Burn any of them completely, and the
carbon in it ends up as carbon dioxide.

4
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.170
Now suppose you need
the same heat from each.

5
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.670
Would they all put out the
same amount of carbon dioxide?

6
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:25.930
Coal, oil, gas: for the same heat,
which puts out the least carbon dioxide?

7
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:30.110
In this mission, you'll compare fuels
by the energy they release per gram,

8
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.730
and the carbon dioxide they
give out per kilojoule.

9
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:39.370
You'll see how carbon dioxide warms the
planet, and weigh up the case for biofuels.

10
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:40.430
Your mission:

11
00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:45.790
find out which fossil fuel gives the least
carbon dioxide for the same heat, and why.
